---

## Definition of Done

A documentation item is considered complete when:

- Source code has been reviewed.
- Component responsibilities are documented.
- Dependencies are identified.
- Execution flows are documented.
- Algorithms and decision logic are explained.
- Relevant architecture or UML diagrams are added.
- Technical risks and limitations are identified.
- Unverified assumptions are clearly indicated.
- The documentation is published in the Wiki.
- The documentation is reviewed by the team.

---

## Current Focus

Technology Stack and External Dependencies.

